<InfoPage title="Editorial Policy" kicker="How we publish" description="Standards for original Spicy Chat AI comparisons, primary sources, updates, adult boundaries, and corrections."><h2>Useful before optimized</h2><p>Every page must answer a real reader question. Keywords belong in clear titles, headings, and natural explanations—not repetition or hidden blocks.</p><h2>Primary sources</h2><p>Product claims link directly to SpicyChat documentation and official competitor pages where possible; a citation never redirects to a promotional destination. We distinguish active context from semantic memory, avoid treating marketing as test results, and require live verification for changing tiers and models.</p><h2>Promotional links</h2><p>A clearly labeled Playbox referral link appears in the English footer. Its referral parameter is separate from cited sources and comparison verdicts; it is not an official SpicyChat link or an endorsement by SpicyChat.</p><h2>Adult boundaries</h2><p>Coverage concerns adults and emphasizes consenting fictional scenarios, privacy, cost visibility, and emotional boundaries. We never request private chats, credentials, saved memories, or intimate personal images.</p><h2>Corrections</h2><p>Material corrections update the article and its machine-readable modification date. Requests should identify the URL, disputed statement, and a direct source supporting the correction.</p></InfoPage>
